{
  "_schema": "Motors publish a headline thrust figure that is only meaningful alongside the prop and pack it was measured with, so 'thrust_test' names both. That is what lets the sim fit the thrust coefficient k_t from real data (physics.md §4: do not guess C_T) instead of inventing one, and what lets the same motor produce more thrust on 6S without any extra data. EVERY motor must carry a thrust_test whose prop_id exists in propellers.json — a typo there does not make the drone slightly wrong, it fits k_t against an empty dictionary; tests/test_parts_system.gd guards this. 'poles' is carried for the electrical-frequency observable (a 14-pole motor has 7 pole pairs); no consumer reads it yet, and it is kept because it is a real spec of a real motor, not because something depends on it. Two tiers, as in frames.json: `specs` is physics-bearing, `catalog` is browsing metadata only, and colour, price and vendor links are banned by name from both. Entries are ordered by stator size then KV, which is what gives the stator filter an ascending order without anything sorting it.",
